const faqs = [
  { question: 'What causes tight hips?', answer: 'A feeling of hip tightness can come from many things, including long periods in one position, training fatigue, limited movement variety or simply the way a person perceives tension. It does not always mean a muscle is physically shortened.' },
  { question: 'How often can I do hip mobility?', answer: 'Short, comfortable mobility work can often be used several times per week. The right frequency depends on how the movements feel, your training schedule and whether symptoms improve, stay the same or worsen.' },
  { question: 'Should hip mobility hurt?', answer: 'No. Mild muscular effort or stretch sensation can be normal, but sharp, pinching, radiating or worsening pain is a reason to stop and get appropriate guidance.' },
  { question: 'Is stretching enough for hip mobility?', answer: 'Not always. Mobility includes both available range and control. Combining gentle range-of-motion work with strength through comfortable positions is often more useful than passive stretching alone.' }
];

